<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA) — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Indian Contract Act 1872, Specific Relief Act 1963</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>₹100 to ₹200 Non-Judicial e-Stamp Paper in Karnataka</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Not compulsory; Binding inter-parties contract</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Optional; Notarization strengthens evidentiary value in civil court</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Civil Courts of jurisdiction agreed between the parties (e.g. Bengaluru)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>3 years from the date of discovered breach of confidentiality</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Company Incorporation / CIN details of corporate parties; Board Resolution authorizing signatories; PAN Card and ID proofs of individual signatories</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">NON-DISCLOSURE AGREEMENT (NDA)</div>
<div class="draft-body">MUTUAL NON-DISCLOSURE AND CONFIDENTIALITY AGREEMENT

This MUTUAL NON-DISCLOSURE AGREEMENT (the "Agreement") is made on this _____ day of _______________, 2026, by and between:

PARTY A: __________________________________________________, having address at ______________________________________________________________________;
AND
PARTY B: __________________________________________________, having address at ______________________________________________________________________.

1. PURPOSE:
The parties wish to explore a potential business relationship / collaboration regarding ____________________________________________________ (the "Purpose").

2. CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION:
"Confidential Information" refers to all proprietary data, financial figures, customer information, trade secrets, software algorithms, source code, designs, and business plans disclosed by either party.

3. OBLIGATIONS:
The Receiving Party agrees to maintain strict confidentiality, limit access to employees on need-to-know basis, and not disclose Confidential Information to any third party without prior written consent.

4. EXCLUSIONS:
Confidential Information does not include information that is publicly known through no breach, already known prior to disclosure, or required to be disclosed by court order.

5. TERM:
This Agreement and the confidentiality obligations shall remain in effect for 3 (three) years from the date of execution.

6. INJUNCTION:
Both parties acknowledge that damages alone would be inadequate compensation for a breach, and the Disclosing Party shall be entitled to seek injunctive relief.

7. GOVERNING LAW:
Governed by Indian Law; Courts in ________________________, Karnataka shall have exclusive jurisdiction.

PARTY A: ___________________________           PARTY B: ___________________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>